Package: fusednet
Type: Package
Title: Fast Sparse Fused Lasso Paths for Generalised Linear and Cox
        Models
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Md Mehedi Hasan", family = "Bhuiyan", email = "309mdhasan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits sparse fused lasso penalised regression models over a path
    of regularisation parameters, in the style of 'glmnet'. Supported models are
    linear, logistic, Poisson, negative binomial (with fixed or estimated
    dispersion) and Cox proportional hazards regression (Breslow ties). The
    penalty is lambda1 * sum|beta_j| + lambda2 * sum|beta_{j+1} - beta_j|.
    The core solver is written in C++ (via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo') and uses
    accelerated proximal gradient descent (FISTA with adaptive restart) where
    the proximal step is computed exactly in linear time with Condat's direct
    total-variation algorithm, together with warm starts along the path, an
    exact lambda_max computation, cross-validation, prediction and plotting.
    Methods: Tibshirani et al. (2005) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9868.2005.00490.x>,
    Beck and Teboulle (2009) <doi:10.1137/080716542>, Condat (2013)
    <doi:10.1109/LSP.2013.2278339>.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), stats, graphics, parallel
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), glmnet, survival, MASS
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
URL: https://github.com/mmhb100/fusednet
BugReports: https://github.com/mmhb100/fusednet/issues
